2026-09-01T19:52:00.000Z note (out-of-band: the exhaustion-gate ruling in this ticket's body was written by hand at 19:30, between iteration 2 and the retry, and finish() reverted it at 19:49 as expected — the engine snapshots ticket.meta AND ticket.body at run start and backlog.write() renders both back from that snapshot (spike/src/backlog.js:86-88). It was re-applied afterwards onto the run's own frontmatter, so stage=requirements and the history entry are the engine's and only the body is the hand edit. The sequence is deliberate and worth copying: head-of-product reads ticket.md FROM DISK when its prompt is built, so a mid-run body edit does reach the next iteration; it just does not survive the run. That is what made the retry productive rather than a repeat — iteration 2 recorded that it had opened on an unchanged tree and could not rule its own blocker, iteration 3 opened on a changed one and returned ready. Ruud answered retry against a recommendation to advance, and was right: the recommendation assumed the tree would stay unchanged, which was a thing to fix rather than a fact to accept.)
